== cafe | AFTERNOON · CAMPUS CAFÉ | busy campus coffee shop with chalkboard menu and warm lights | cafe +laptop
ade (cheer): Quddus! I emailed fifty professors for a funded PhD! Same email, I just changed the name.
quddus (think): And how many replied?
ade (facepalm): Zero. One autoreply. It said the professor is on holiday until 2029.
quddus (talk): Professors can tell when an email was sent to fifty people. Let's fix it.
ade (think): Okay. What should I write?

== office | LATER · STUDY ROOM | quiet modern study room with a whiteboard, books and a laptop | desk @ade
quddus (point): First, a clear subject line. For example: prospective PhD student, interest in your work on solar batteries.
> 1f4e9 | THE EMAIL | 1f4cc Clear subject line | 1f4da Mention a paper of theirs you read | 1f4c8 Your skills that match, briefly | 2753 Ask if they're taking students
ade (type): Then I introduce myself?
quddus (talk): In two lines. Then mention one of their recent papers and what interested you. Show you actually read it.
ade (worried): And then I ask them for money?
quddus (talk): No. Ask if they are accepting PhD students next year, and if funding is available. Attach your CV. Keep it short.
ade (think): So, one professor, one personal email, not fifty copies.
quddus (thumbs): Exactly. Quality beats quantity.
ade (cheer): Sending one perfect email. And no more holiday autoreplies, please!
